WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:15.227
<v Host>Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June first. Today's story is a Japanese custom: June first is the day people switch to their summer clothes. Let's listen.

00:00:15.827 --> 00:00:18.588
<v News>今日のニュースです。

00:00:19.288 --> 00:00:23.295
<v News>今日は、6月1日です。

00:00:23.995 --> 00:00:28.891
<v News>6月1日は、「衣替え」の日です。

00:00:29.591 --> 00:00:34.103
<v News>「衣替え」は、服を変えることです。

00:00:34.804 --> 00:00:38.188
<v News>暑い季節になりました。

00:00:38.887 --> 00:00:42.871
<v News>だから、夏の服に変えます。

00:00:43.572 --> 00:00:47.411
<v News>夏の服は、すずしいです。

00:00:48.112 --> 00:00:53.008
<v News>多くの学校で、夏の制服になります。

00:00:53.707 --> 00:00:58.844
<v News>会社でも、夏の服を着る人が多いです。

00:00:59.543 --> 00:01:04.799
<v News>「衣替え」は、昔から続く習慣です。

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:09.459
<v News>平安時代に、始まりました。

00:01:10.159 --> 00:01:15.224
<v News>10月1日は、冬の服に変えます。

00:01:15.924 --> 00:01:20.099
<v News>暑い日も、寒い日も、あります。

00:01:20.799 --> 00:01:25.504
<v News>だから、ゆっくり変える学校もあります。

00:01:26.203 --> 00:01:30.884
<v News>日本の、季節を感じる習慣です。

00:01:31.584 --> 00:01:33.215
<v Host>Let's break it down.

00:01:33.816 --> 00:01:38.376
<v Slow>今日は、6月1日です。

00:01:39.176 --> 00:01:41.504
<v Host>Today is June first.

00:01:42.103 --> 00:01:44.120
<v Vocab>今日

00:01:44.519 --> 00:01:49.343
<v Host>It means today. One of the very first words every learner picks up.

00:01:49.944 --> 00:01:55.536
<v Slow>6月1日は、「衣替え」の日です。

00:01:56.335 --> 00:02:00.224
<v Host>June first is the day for changing clothes by season.

00:02:00.823 --> 00:02:03.319
<v Vocab>衣替え

00:02:03.719 --> 00:02:10.367
<v Host>It names the custom of switching your wardrobe when the season changes. The first part means clothing.

00:02:10.967 --> 00:02:16.127
<v Slow>「衣替え」は、服を変えることです。

00:02:16.927 --> 00:02:19.472
<v Host>It is the act of changing your clothes.

00:02:20.072 --> 00:02:22.039
<v Vocab>服

00:02:22.439 --> 00:02:26.328
<v Host>It means clothes. Use it for clothing in general.

00:02:26.927 --> 00:02:30.792
<v Slow>暑い季節になりました。

00:02:31.592 --> 00:02:33.752
<v Host>It has become the hot season.

00:02:34.352 --> 00:02:36.560
<v Vocab>暑い

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:41.975
<v Host>It means hot, for the weather. A must-know word for a Japanese summer.

00:02:42.575 --> 00:02:47.111
<v Slow>だから、夏の服に変えます。

00:02:47.912 --> 00:02:51.151
<v Host>So, people change into summer clothes.

00:02:51.752 --> 00:02:53.840
<v Vocab>夏

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:59.159
<v Host>It means summer. The four seasons are a favorite topic in Japanese.

00:02:59.759 --> 00:03:04.151
<v Slow>夏の服は、すずしいです。

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.824
<v Host>Summer clothes are cool.

00:03:07.424 --> 00:03:09.943
<v Vocab>涼しい

00:03:10.343 --> 00:03:16.680
<v Host>It means cool in a pleasant way, the opposite of hot. Perfect for describing a nice breeze.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:22.872
<v Slow>多くの学校で、夏の制服になります。

00:03:23.671 --> 00:03:27.776
<v Host>At many schools, the uniform becomes the summer one.

00:03:28.376 --> 00:03:30.776
<v Vocab>制服

00:03:31.175 --> 00:03:37.223
<v Host>It means uniform, like the ones students wear. Japanese schools are famous for them.

00:03:37.824 --> 00:03:43.680
<v Slow>会社でも、夏の服を着る人が多いです。

00:03:44.479 --> 00:03:48.415
<v Host>At companies too, many people wear summer clothes.

00:03:49.015 --> 00:03:50.984
<v Vocab>着る

00:03:51.383 --> 00:03:57.360
<v Host>It means to wear, for clothes on the upper body. A very common everyday verb.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:03.984
<v Slow>「衣替え」は、昔から続く習慣です。

00:04:04.783 --> 00:04:09.728
<v Host>Changing clothes by season is a custom that has continued since long ago.

00:04:10.328 --> 00:04:12.656
<v Vocab>習慣

00:04:13.056 --> 00:04:17.160
<v Host>It means a custom or habit, something people do regularly.

00:04:17.759 --> 00:04:22.271
<v Slow>平安時代に、始まりました。

00:04:23.072 --> 00:04:27.319
<v Host>It began in the Heian period, about a thousand years ago.

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:30.247
<v Vocab>始まる

00:04:30.648 --> 00:04:35.687
<v Host>It means to begin or to start. The thing itself starts, on its own.

00:04:36.288 --> 00:04:41.639
<v Slow>日本の、季節を感じる習慣です。

00:04:42.439 --> 00:04:46.016
<v Host>It is a custom that lets you feel the seasons of Japan.

00:04:46.615 --> 00:04:48.848
<v Vocab>季節

00:04:49.247 --> 00:04:53.567
<v Host>It means season. Japan makes a big deal of all four.

00:04:54.168 --> 00:04:57.168
<v Host>Let's listen to the full story one more time.

00:04:57.767 --> 00:05:00.528
<v News>今日のニュースです。

00:05:01.228 --> 00:05:05.235
<v News>今日は、6月1日です。

00:05:05.935 --> 00:05:10.831
<v News>6月1日は、「衣替え」の日です。

00:05:11.531 --> 00:05:16.043
<v News>「衣替え」は、服を変えることです。

00:05:16.744 --> 00:05:20.127
<v News>暑い季節になりました。

00:05:20.827 --> 00:05:24.812
<v News>だから、夏の服に変えます。

00:05:25.512 --> 00:05:29.351
<v News>夏の服は、すずしいです。

00:05:30.052 --> 00:05:34.947
<v News>多くの学校で、夏の制服になります。

00:05:35.648 --> 00:05:40.783
<v News>会社でも、夏の服を着る人が多いです。

00:05:41.483 --> 00:05:46.740
<v News>「衣替え」は、昔から続く習慣です。

00:05:47.439 --> 00:05:51.399
<v News>平安時代に、始まりました。

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:57.163
<v News>10月1日は、冬の服に変えます。

00:05:57.863 --> 00:06:02.040
<v News>暑い日も、寒い日も、あります。

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:07.444
<v News>だから、ゆっくり変える学校もあります。

00:06:08.144 --> 00:06:12.824
<v News>日本の、季節を感じる習慣です。

00:06:13.524 --> 00:06:16.211
<v Host>Quiz time. Four questions.

00:06:16.812 --> 00:06:20.627
<v Slow>今日は、何の日ですか。

00:06:21.427 --> 00:06:25.459
<v Host>What day is today? It is the day to switch to summer clothes.

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:31.795
<v Slow>6月1日は、どんな服に変えますか。

00:06:32.596 --> 00:06:37.516
<v Host>What kind of clothes do people change into on June first? Summer clothes.

00:06:38.115 --> 00:06:43.468
<v Slow>「衣替え」は、いつ始まりましたか。

00:06:44.267 --> 00:06:48.971
<v Host>When did this custom begin? In the Heian period, long ago.

00:06:49.572 --> 00:06:55.451
<v Slow>10月1日は、どんな服に変えますか。

00:06:56.252 --> 00:07:01.244
<v Host>What clothes do people change into on October first? Winter clothes.

00:07:01.843 --> 00:07:14.228
<v Host>That's today's Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

00:07:14.827 --> 00:07:17.084
<v News>また明日。
